{
  "name": "Walls round plans",
  "_about": "WALLS ROUND ANY PLAN (`enclosure`): each edge of the outline a wall face with its own openings, the faces meeting on their mitres -- a square hall, the chamfered square of the Taj Mahal or the Frauenkirche, an octagonal baptistery. `openings` is every face's (a pattern, centred on the face) and `faces` overrides it by face. A round window is an opening with a FOOT as well as a head -- a semicircle under a semicircle -- and a rose is a big one. Beside them: a PRISM on the same kinds of plan (a plinth), FLYING BUTTRESSES (a strut on a rampant quarter-arch from a pier to the wall), and BELL domes (concave below the waist, convex above it -- `waist` and `lift` say where it turns: the Frauenkirche's stone bell).",
